ainst UT Martin at Milan Puskar Stadium on Sept. 12, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/12/_DSC9769.jpeg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 11:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59383</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers to Cap Nonconference Slate Against UConn Sunday</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/12/womens-soccer-mountaineers-to-cap-nonconference-slate-against-uconn-sunday</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/12/womens-soccer-mountaineers-to-cap-nonconference-slate-against-uconn-sunday</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Alina Gnädig prepares to pass a ball during a game at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/11/TT_WSOC_WVUvsDuquesne_52.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The No. 8-ranked West Virginia University women's soccer team prepares to conclude the nonconference portion of its schedule when it welcomes UConn to Morgantown on Sunday, Sept. 13. Kickoff at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium is set for 1 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/TT_WSOC_WVUvsDuquesne_52.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/TT_WSOC_WVUvsDuquesne_52.jpg"><media:title>Alina Gnädig prepares to pass a ball during a game at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/TT_WSOC_WVUvsDuquesne_52.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:30:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59382</s:story_id></item><item><title>Countdown to Kickoff: Mountaineers to Face UT Martin Today</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/12/football-countdown-to-kickoff-mountaineers-to-face-ut-martin-today</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/9/12/football-countdown-to-kickoff-mountaineers-to-face-ut-martin-today</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia coach Rich Rodriguez visits with media in the Milan Puskar Center Team Room on Tuesday, Sept.10, ahead of the Mountaineers' meeting with UT Martin." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/9/11/Rodriguez-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – West Virginia is seeking its first 2-0 start to a season in eight years on Saturday afternoon when it faces UT Martin at Milan Puskar Stadium.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/Rodriguez-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/Rodriguez-Main.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia coach Rich Rodriguez visits with media in the Milan Puskar Center Team Room on Tuesday, Sept.10, ahead of the Mountaineers' meeting with UT Martin.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/9/11/Rodriguez-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59384</s:story_id></item></channel></rss>